39	2	# Weekly Client Summary – Period Ending June 19, 2026\r\n\r\nThis week, work shifted between finalizing the **Stellar Docs Web Migration** and implementing several important refinements to the **Therapy Order Automation** system based on feedback from Stephanie’s latest run.\r\n\r\n### Therapy Order Automation\r\n**Status: Updates Deployed (Release 1.2.0)**\r\nStephanie’s team completed a full round of IEP Therapy Orders, which provided valuable real-world data. Based on that feedback, I’ve implemented and deployed several fixes to make the process more reliable for the next big send-out in September:\r\n\r\n*   **District Filtering:** I added a new feature that allows Jake to limit order generation to specific districts. By providing a list of district IDs, you can now perform "special" send-outs without processing the entire database.\r\n*   **PDF Layout Fix:** We identified that long email addresses were pushing some order forms onto a second page. I adjusted the header and column widths to ensure everything fits on a single page, even with long contact details.\r\n*   **Improved Exclusion Logic:** To prevent duplicate or unnecessary orders, the system now automatically excludes students with a status of "Sent-Waiting on Response," "Moved out of District," or "Inactive Student."\r\n*   **Next Steps for Automation:** I am still working on two remaining items from Stephanie’s list:\r\n    *   Updating the logic to ensure the "last seen" therapist is selected rather than the "most seen."\r\n    *   Ensuring the system continues looking for a "present" visit if the most recent session was marked "absent."\r\n\r\n### Stellar Docs: Web Migration & Renovations\r\n**Status: Testing & Awaiting Approval**\r\nI am continuing to move through therapist workflows (interventions and reports) in the test environment to ensure 100% accuracy. \r\n\r\n*   **Bug Squashing:** I’ve been working through the scripting issues identified last week, specifically the date-picker conflict and the "Enter Details" button error.\r\n*   **Refinement:** The "pruning" of old, commented-out code continues as I move through each module, which is significantly cleaning up the back-end of the new site.\r\n\r\n### Eligibility Verifications\r\n**Status: Operational & Stable**\r\n*   The system remains stable with no issues to report.\r\n\r\n### Pending Questions (Blockers for Migration)\r\nTo hit our rollout targets, I still need your feedback on these three items:\r\n\r\n1.  **Production Switch:** Are we still aiming for a mid-June/late-June move to production? I need to finalize the downtime window once you approve the plan.\r\n2.  **"Add Student" Workflow:** Can we confirm if the "Add Student" feature in Stellar Docs is now redundant because of the "Hub"? If so, I will disable it to keep the interface clean.\r\n3.  **Database & UI Updates:** I am still awaiting approval for the **Soft Delete** database changes and the **UI display updates** for intervention items.\r\n\r\n### Next Steps\r\n*   **Complete Therapy Order Tweaks:** Finalize the logic for "last seen" therapists and "absent" visits.\r\n*   **Final Migration Checklist:** Once I receive the approvals mentioned above, I will prepare the final checklist for the live move.\r\n*   **Workflow Verification:** Continue rigorous testing of the report generation features in the migrated environment.	2026-06-19 21:51:32.5078+00	2026-06-19 21:51:32.5078+00
40	3	# Client Summary: Tex Tech\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nThis week, we hit a major milestone with the release of **v3.17.1**. This update includes the new "Worksheet" view for the Material Review Board (MRB) in beta, the visual note alerts we discussed, and several requested interface improvements. Most of the technical heavy lifting for the MRB transition is complete, and we are now in a phase of monitoring user feedback and waiting for a few data examples to resolve remaining troubleshooting items.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Now Live: MRB "Worksheet" & Visual Alerts\r\nThe updated MRB system is now available for the team to use.\r\n*   **The New Worksheet View (Beta):** We have deployed the spreadsheet-style interface. To ensure no one is slowed down while they learn the new layout, I’ve added a **Beta/Classic Toggle**. Users can jump back and forth between the old view and the new one as needed.\r\n*   **New Interaction Layout:** Based on the rework, the new view replaces the clunky buttons on every row with a focus panel on the right side. When you click a cell, the panel updates to show disposition options and notes for that specific sample.\r\n*   **Visual Note Alerts:** The "paperclip" icon now changes from blue to yellow instantly whenever a note is added. This is live in both the Classic and Worksheet views.\r\n*   **Real-Time Updates:** I fixed the logic issues with the background sync (SignalR). Now, when one user makes a disposition or adds a note, the change should appear on everyone else’s screen immediately without needing a page refresh.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Completed This Period\r\n*   **Test Renaming:** The "Elongation Bias" test has been officially renamed to **"Elongation @ 2lbs – Bias"** across the system. This included updating the definitions, existing observations, and style configurations.\r\n*   **Work Order UI Tweaks:** I’ve updated the New Work Order screen to require a frame number and added a suggestion list for style selection to reduce data entry errors.\r\n*   **Note Deletion:** I’ve added a "Delete Note" function to the backlog for the work-app to help users clean up accidental entries.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Troubleshooting: Master Roll Truncation\r\nI am still standing by for example data from the Operations team regarding the **10-digit roll numbers** that are being cut off. Once I have a few specific examples of the failed numbers, I can apply the fix to the identification logic.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Pending Decisions (Blockers)\r\nWe are still looking for a steer on these three items to keep them moving forward:\r\n1.  **Yardage Clock:** Do we proceed with the Windows communication method (Option A) or the Raspberry Pi bridge (Option B)?\r\n2.  **Data Management:** Should I build a "Quarterly Archive" feature, or would you prefer a straightforward "Data Retention/Deletion" policy?\r\n3.  **Search Speed:** We need to decide if the "roll status" summary is a "must-have" for daily searches. If it is, I’ll need to schedule time to build background tables to prevent the search from becoming sluggish.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Next Steps\r\n*   **Monitor Beta Feedback:** I’ll be watching for any issues as the team experiments with the Worksheet view and the Beta toggle.\r\n*   **Edge-Case Testing:** Continuing to refine automated tests for complex MRB dispositions (like "Scrap" rules that affect rolls before/after a sample).\r\n*   **Documentation:** I am continuing to document test cases and architecture to ensure the system remains maintainable long-term.	2026-06-19 21:59:23.885568+00	2026-06-19 21:59:23.885568+00
