144	194	2026-03-26T20:56:35.239Z	text/markdown	Corrected in release 1.0.2	Release correction note	2026-03-26 20:56:44.538367+00	2026-03-26 20:56:44.538367+00
11	64	2025-12-12T22:25:50.915Z	text/markdown	I've been exploring different options for how to create and publish the PDFs. I had seen some indications—or maybe it was an AI hallucination (I did talk to Gemini about this stuff)—that we might be able to save some API costs by pre-embedding the AcroForm signature field in the PDF. So far that hasn't turned out to be the case, at least not for DocuSign or PandaDoc. Maybe it will be for the cheaper signing providers, but I don't know if Holly's going to be interested in working with them.\r\n\r\nMy recommendation to her for now was to develop the PDF using a free library and plan to have the signing platform add the signature field. If we end up needing to go with IronPDF or Apryse, we'll have to rewrite the PDF code, but I bet AI could do that pretty easily.	PDF generation and e-signature field strategy	2025-12-12 22:28:18.888+00	2025-12-12 22:28:18.888+00
12	64	2025-12-29T22:21:25.479Z	text/markdown	I spent some time last Friday and again today adding the QuestPDF code. I've got the basic structure set up, but Gemini is tripping a little bit on the information it's giving me, so I'm going to switch to Claude and hopefully get some things cleaned up.\r\n\r\nI added Verify to do snapshot testing. I think that's going to be a good approach. Direct unit testing isn't exactly a thing.\r\n\r\nNext step, clean up the errors that are causing the tests to fail, then visually inspect the output of the test and adjust the code until the PDF looks right.\r\n\r\nAfter that, need to give some thought to how to QA this process as part of the monthly run.	QuestPDF integration and testing development progress	2025-12-29 22:23:15.766+00	2025-12-29 22:23:15.766+00
13	64	2026-01-01T19:54:07.068Z	text/markdown	I've got the PDF generation to a point where it mostly sort of matches the sample, with a few weird spacing and layout things still to address.\r\n\r\nNext step is to set up some test data and generate some sample PDFs to send to Stellar to review.\r\n\r\nAfter that I need to give some thought to the QA process.	PDF generation progress and next steps	2026-01-01 19:55:02.736+00	2026-01-01 19:55:02.736+00
14	64	2026-01-09T22:34:43.074Z	text/markdown	I've added a lot more of the batch process code, especially the database connection stuff.\r\n\r\nFor some reason it's not creating the directory. And there's some weirdness about how it's logging out the results. I need to check on that next.	Batch process code development and current issues	2026-01-09 22:35:27.772+00	2026-01-09 22:35:27.772+00
15	64	2026-01-13T00:18:29.929Z	text/markdown	The PDF layout looks really close to right. I sent Holly, Stephanie, and Melissa a few samples to review.\r\n\r\nI broke my unit tests with the database repository stuff I added the other day. They need an `IConfiguration`. I don't want to create that. I'm going to switch to creating an `AppConfig` structure and using that to hold the connection string and whatever else. I may also peel off a layer or two of repository abstraction if I can. I may have overdone that.	Development update on PDF layout, unit tests, and configuration changes	2026-01-13 00:20:17.273+00	2026-01-13 00:20:17.273+00
16	64	2026-01-15T22:10:57.337Z	text/markdown	I can't think of anything else to do with this. The PDF layout has been reviewed and seems to be OK. The tests are all passing.	PDF layout reviewed, tests passing	2026-01-15 22:11:49.996+00	2026-01-15 22:11:49.996+00
