55	46	2026-02-06T17:44:22.460Z	text/markdown	I was able to get the test site fully operational. It's like 95% of the way there on the initial run via Terraform, and then there's always a little bit of manual stuff. \r\n\r\nThe test site is an essential component of this process because I need to be confident that each individual item that I migrate will behave correctly.\r\n\r\nI created some work items to try to make the automated processes more idempotent so that I can rerun parts of it without having to wait for the full half-hour-long teardown and rebuild process.	Operational test site and efforts to improve automation idempotency	2026-02-06 17:45:45.758+00	2026-02-06 18:32:30.633+00
56	38	2025-11-06T21:57:58.517Z	text/markdown	This is my response to Holly's initial proposal:\r\n\r\nI don’t see any reason we shouldn’t be able to almost completely automate the therapy orders. The basic process would consist of:\r\n\r\nA monthly job that would create therapist referral records in Stellar Docs based on the criteria you outlined and then use DocuSign to create and send the envelopes\r\nSome kind of process for monitoring the responses, which would then update Stellar Docs with the results\r\nA way of handling non-responses\r\nA way of flagging therapists not to send to again\r\nA way of generating and sending the “heads-up” email\r\n\r\nPulling the data is detailed but seems straightforward enough. \r\n\r\nFor generating the documents, we can get by without Doc Creator. If practical, the simplest option would be to set up a template in DocuSign. If that won’t work, we could write C# code to create the PDFs directly from the data (there are good free PDF libraries).\r\n\r\nMonitoring can be either “pull" or “push". Pull would be a (daily?) batch job that would use the DocuSign API to check for responses. Push would be an endpoint we set up for DocuSign to send responses to. That could be either an API that we set up for that purpose (which could be really really useful for the admin changes and other things) or it could be something like an AWS lambda that drops a message in a queue that we could monitor via the StellarAutomationSupport service we implemented as part of the eligibility verifications. Either way, we would take the response and then update Stellar Docs based on the results.\r\n\r\nNon-responses and flagging therapists could probably be part of the monthly job, actually. Just need a little more detail on exactly how that works.\r\n\r\nGenerating the heads-up email could be done automatically. Not sure if you guys already have an email service that you use, but there are a number of options. Or we could generate a report and somebody could send those manually if preferred.\r\n\r\nThis would require you to pay for the DocuSign API. Not sure how big of an expense that would be relative to what you’re paying now.\r\n\r\nI’m not quite at a point where I’m ready to provide an estimate. I need to take a little time to dig into the reports you’re pulling to understand the data. Also, could you please tell me a little more about how importing the results works (step 12 in your instructions)? And if you could send me the form template(s), that would also be really helpful.	Response to therapy order automation proposal	2025-11-06 21:58:43.618+00	2025-11-06 21:58:43.618+00
