68	118	2026-01-30T18:55:39.138Z	text/markdown	***discussion***\r\n\r\nThis please!\r\n_A separate table could also make sense. If we were going to do that, I would probably recommend that it be designed around the “Not Accepting” therapists. Basically a therapist ID and a “Not Accepting” reason (could be freeform). _\r\n\r\nThis is a reply or forward from Holly Christopher.  \r\n\r\nholly@stellartherapy.com\r\n(423) 708-2661\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOn Fri, Jan 30, 2026 at 1:49 PM Michael Gant <jmgant@cleareyeconsulting.com> wrote:\r\nI set it up as a required field but with a default value of Accepting, so there won't be any nulls. Is that OK?\r\n\r\nA separate table could also make sense. If we were going to do that, I would probably recommend that it be designed around the “Not Accepting” therapists. Basically a therapist ID and a “Not Accepting” reason (could be freeform). \r\n\r\nFor some reason I was thinking there was a preference for having an explicit Accepting or Not Accepting for every therapist record. But at least based on what I know of the process, a THERAPISTS_NOT_ACCEPTING_ORDERS table seems like the simplest option for you guys to manage, and it’s all the same to me as far as the query.\r\n\r\nIt’s already built the other way, of course, but it wouldn’t take more than an hour to switch it.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOn Jan 29, 2026, at 6:39 PM, Holly Christopher <holly@stellartherapy.com> wrote:\r\n\r\nIt should not affect anything as long as it is not a required field. If you want to make it a new table and join them that is fine too. \r\n\r\nThis is a reply or forward from Holly Christopher.  \r\n\r\nholly@stellartherapy.com\r\n(423) 708-2661\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nOn Thu, Jan 29, 2026 at 2:11 PM Michael Gant <jmgant@cleareyeconsulting.com> wrote:\r\nSorry, I meant to add…\r\n\r\nI’d be happy to do the database change. It should just take a second. I just have never added a column to the THERAPISTS table before and I wanted to make sure it wasn’t going to break any reports or anything. Does anybody know whether adding columns to that table in the past has had any ill effects?	Discussion about therapist availability database changes	2026-01-30 18:56:49.075+00	2026-01-30 18:56:49.075+00
69	58	2025-12-04T18:52:31.931Z	text/markdown	Sample extract query:\r\n\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nIF OBJECT_ID(N'tempdb..#TherapistCred') IS NOT NULL DROP TABLE #TherapistCred\r\nIF OBJECT_ID(N'tempdb..#SupervisorData') IS NOT NULL DROP TABLE #SupervisorData\r\n\r\nSELECT distinct\r\nE.EV_EVENT_ID,\r\nE.EV_EVENTSTART,\r\nE.EV_EVENTEND,\r\nE.EV_SchoolID,\r\n--E.EV_EVENT_TYPE_ID,\r\n    ATT_STUDENT_ID,\r\n\tCASE \r\n        WHEN TE.THE_CredTherStatus_ID IS NULL THEN NULL\r\n        ELSE ESO_SIGNER_ID\r\n    END AS ESO_SIGNER_ID,\r\n\tSE.SER_SERVICES_ID as ESO_SER,\r\n\tDE.DISC_Discipline_ID as ESO_DISC_ID,\r\n\tDE.DISC_Abbrev as ESO_DISC_ABB,\r\n\tCASE \r\n        WHEN TA.THE_CredTherStatus_ID IS NULL THEN NULL\r\n        ELSE ATT_Supervisor_ID\r\n    END AS ATT_Supervisor_ID,\r\n\tSA.SER_SERVICES_ID as ATT_SER,\r\n\tDA.DISC_Discipline_ID as ATT_DISC_ID,\r\n\tDA.DISC_Abbrev as ATT_DISC_ABB,\r\n\tEV_THERAPIST_ID,\r\n\tS.SER_SERVICES_ID as THER_SER,\r\n\tDT.DISC_Discipline_ID as THER_DISC_ID,\r\n\tDT.DISC_Abbrev as THER_DISC_ABB,\r\n\tREF_ID,\r\n\tREFSTATUS_ID,\r\n\tREF_SERVICE_ID,\r\n\tSVA_SERVICES_ID,\r\n\tTS.SER_Discipline as IEP_Service_Type,\r\n\tIEP_IEP_ID,\r\n\tIEP_BeginningDate,\r\n\tIEP_EndingDate,\r\n\t--DO.DOC_DOCTOR_ORDERS_ID,\r\n\t--ISA.SVA_Services_Assign_ID,\r\n\t--DOSTATUS_DESCRIPTION,\r\n\t--DO.DOC_PHYSICIANS_ID,\r\n\tD.DIS_DISTRICTS_ID,\r\n\tD.DIS_Name,\r\n    SCH_Name,\r\n\tSAS_Ending_Date\r\n\r\ninto #TherapistCred\r\nFROM EVENT E\r\nleft JOIN EVENT_SIGN_OFF\r\n    ON ESO_EVENT_ID = EV_EVENT_ID\r\nJOIN ATTENDANCE A\r\n    ON EV_EVENT_ID = ATT_EVENT_ID\r\n    AND ATT_ATTENDANCESTATUS = 'Present'\r\nLEFT JOIN EVENT_TYPE\r\n    ON EV_EVENT_TYPE_ID = ETP_EVENT_TYPE_ID\r\nJOIN IEP IEP\r\n    ON ATT_STUDENT_ID = IEP.IEP_STUDENT_ID\r\n\tAND EV_Eventstart BETWEEN IEP.IEP_BeginningDate AND IEP.IEP_EndingDate\r\nJOIN IEP_SERVICE_ASSIGNMENTS ISA \r\n    ON ISA.SVA_IEP_ID = IEP.IEP_IEP_ID\r\nJOIN EVENT_TYPE ET\r\n    ON E.EV_Event_Type_id = ET.ETP_EVENT_TYPE_ID\r\nLEFT JOIN DOCTOR_ORDERS DO \r\n    ON DO.SVA_Services_Assign_ID = ISA.SVA_SERVICES_ASSIGN_ID\r\nLEFT JOIN DOCORDER_STATUS \r\n    ON DOSTATUS_ID = DO.DOC_DOSTATUS_ID \r\n    --AND DOSTATUS_ID <> 1\r\nleft JOIN REFERRING_THERAPIST RT\r\n    ON IEP.IEP_IEP_ID = REF_IEP_ID\r\n\tand RT.REF_SERVICE_ID = ISA.SVA_SERVICES_ID\r\nLEFT JOIN REF_THERAPIST_STATUS \r\n    ON REF_STATUS_ID = REFSTATUS_ID\r\n    --AND REFSTATUS_ID IN (14, 3, 4,11)\r\nJOIN INSURANCE_ASSIGNMENTS \r\n    ON IAS_STUDENT_ID = ATT_STUDENT_ID\r\nJOIN INSURANCE \r\n    ON IAS_INSURANCE_ID = INS_INSURANCE_ID\r\n    AND INS_INSURANCE_ID IN (1,2,7,3)\r\nJOIN INSURANCE_TYPE \r\n    ON IAS_TYPE_ID = INS_TYPE_ID\r\n    AND INS_TYPE_ID in (12,13)\r\nleft JOIN dbo.vw_Consents C\r\n    ON C.CST_Student_ID = ATT_STUDENT_ID\r\n\tand C.CST_Signed = 1\r\n\tand C.rn = 1\r\nleft JOIN CONSENTS_NEW CN\r\n    ON CN.CN_Consent_ID = C.CST_CONSENTS_ID\r\n    AND CN.CN_New = 1\r\nJOIN SCHOOLS \r\n    ON SCH_SCHOOLS_ID = E.EV_SchoolID\r\njoin SCHOOL_ASSIGNMENTS\r\n\ton E.EV_SchoolID = SAS_School_ID\r\n\tand ATT_STUDENT_ID = SAS_Student_ID\r\nJOIN DISTRICTS D\r\n    ON SCH_District_ID = DIS_DISTRICTS_ID\r\n    AND DIS_ACTIVE = 1\r\nJOIN Attendance_Treatments\r\n    ON A.ATT_ATTENDANCE_ID = AT_Attendance_ID\r\n    AND AT_Treatment_Code_ID NOT IN (99211, 90000, 80000)\r\nleft JOIN SERVICES TS\r\n    ON TS.SER_SERVICES_ID = ISA.SVA_SERVICES_ID\r\n--event signer\r\nleft JOIN Therapists TE\r\n    ON TE.THE_THERAPISTS_ID = ESO_SIGNER_ID\r\n\tand TE.THE_CredTherStatus_ID in (1,4,5,9)\r\nleft JOIN CREDHealthLicense TEHL\r\n    ON TEHL.CREDHL_THERAPIST_ID = TE.THE_THERAPISTS_ID\r\nleft JOIN CREDLicenseStatus \r\n    ON CREDLicenseStatus_ID = TEHL.CREDHL_CREDSTAT_ID\r\n    AND CREDLicenseStatus_ID NOT IN (2,4,5,6,3)\r\nleft JOIN DISCIPLINES DE\r\n    ON DE.DISC_Discipline_ID = TEHL.CREDHL_LICTYPE\r\n    AND DE.DISC_Discipline_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49)\r\nleft JOIN SERVICES SE\r\n    ON SE.SER_SERVICES_ID = TE.THE_SERVICES_ID\r\n--ATT Supervisor\r\nleft JOIN Therapists TA\r\n    ON TA.THE_THERAPISTS_ID = ATT_Supervisor_ID\r\n\tand TA.THE_CredTherStatus_ID in (1,4,5,9)\r\nleft JOIN CREDHealthLicense TAHL\r\n    ON TAHL.CREDHL_THERAPIST_ID = TA.THE_THERAPISTS_ID\r\nleft JOIN CREDLicenseStatus CA\r\n    ON CA.CREDLicenseStatus_ID = TAHL.CREDHL_CREDSTAT_ID\r\n    AND CA.CREDLicenseStatus_ID NOT IN (2,4,5,6,3)\r\nleft JOIN DISCIPLINES DA\r\n    ON DA.DISC_Discipline_ID = TAHL.CREDHL_LICTYPE\r\n    AND DA.DISC_Discipline_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49)\r\nleft JOIN SERVICES SA\r\n    ON SA.SER_SERVICES_ID = TA.THE_SERVICES_ID\r\n--EV_Therapist\r\nleft JOIN Therapists T\r\n    ON T.THE_THERAPISTS_ID = EV_THERAPIST_ID\r\n\tand T.THE_CredTherStatus_ID in (1,4,5,9)\r\nleft JOIN CREDHealthLicense THL\r\n    ON THL.CREDHL_THERAPIST_ID = T.THE_THERAPISTS_ID\r\nleft JOIN CREDLicenseStatus CT\r\n    ON CT.CREDLicenseStatus_ID = THL.CREDHL_CREDSTAT_ID\r\n    AND CT.CREDLicenseStatus_ID NOT IN (2,4,5,6,3)\r\nleft JOIN DISCIPLINES DT\r\n    ON DT.DISC_Discipline_ID = THL.CREDHL_LICTYPE\r\n    AND DT.DISC_Discipline_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49)\r\nleft JOIN SERVICES S\r\n    ON S.SER_SERVICES_ID = T.THE_SERVICES_ID\r\n\tand S.SER_SERVICES_ID = ISA.SVA_SERVICES_ID\r\nwhere EV_EVENTEND >= DATEADD(DAY, -365, GETDATE())\r\n--and ATT_STUDENT_ID = 415024\r\nAND EV_EVENTEND < GETDATE()\r\n--and RT.REF_ID is null\r\n--and S.SER_SERVICES_ID is not null\r\nand S.SER_SERVICES_ID = ISA.SVA_SERVICES_ID\r\nand (DOC_DOSTATUS_ID <> 1 or DOC_DOSTATUS_ID is null)\r\nAND (REFSTATUS_ID IN (14, 3, 4,11) or RT.REF_ID is null)\r\nand (CST_signed = 1 OR CN_new = 1)\r\nAND E.EV_EVENTSTART BETWEEN @StartDate AND @EndDate \r\nOrder by ATT_STUDENT_ID, IEP_IEP_ID,EV_EVENTSTART;\r\n\r\nSELECT DISTINCT\r\n    TC.ATT_STUDENT_ID,\r\n    MostFrequentTherapist.Therapist_ID AS Supervisor_Therapist_ID,\r\n    TC.IEP_IEP_ID,\r\n    TC.REF_ID,\r\n    TC.REF_SERVICE_ID,\r\n    TC.SVA_services_Id,\r\n    TC.IEP_Service_Type,\r\n    TC.DIS_DISTRICTS_ID,\r\n    TC.DIS_Name,\r\n\tMostRecentEvent.SCH_Name AS School,\r\n    --TC.SCH_Name,\r\n    TC.IEP_BeginningDate,\r\n    TC.IEP_EndingDate\r\ninto #SupervisorData\r\nFROM #TherapistCred TC\r\nCROSS APPLY (\r\n    -- Subquery to find the most frequent therapist\r\n    SELECT TOP 1 \r\n        CASE \r\n            WHEN TC2.ESO_SIGNER_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC2.ESO_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49) THEN TC2.ESO_SIGNER_ID\r\n            WHEN TC2.ATT_Supervisor_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC2.ATT_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49) THEN TC2.ATT_Supervisor_ID\r\n            WHEN TC2.EV_THERAPIST_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC2.THER_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49) THEN TC2.EV_THERAPIST_ID\r\n            ELSE NULL\r\n        END AS Therapist_ID\r\n    FROM #TherapistCred TC2\r\n    WHERE TC2.ATT_STUDENT_ID = TC.ATT_STUDENT_ID\r\n      AND TC2.THER_SER = TC.THER_SER\r\n      AND TC2.IEP_IEP_ID = TC.IEP_IEP_ID\r\n      AND (\r\n          (TC2.ESO_SIGNER_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC2.ESO_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49))\r\n          OR (TC2.ATT_Supervisor_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC2.ATT_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49))\r\n          OR (TC2.EV_THERAPIST_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC2.THER_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49))\r\n      )\r\n    GROUP BY \r\n        CASE \r\n            WHEN TC2.ESO_SIGNER_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC2.ESO_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49) THEN TC2.ESO_SIGNER_ID\r\n            WHEN TC2.ATT_Supervisor_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC2.ATT_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49) THEN TC2.ATT_Supervisor_ID\r\n            WHEN TC2.EV_THERAPIST_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC2.THER_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49) THEN TC2.EV_THERAPIST_ID\r\n            ELSE NULL\r\n        END\r\n    ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC\r\n) MostFrequentTherapist\r\nCROSS APPLY (\r\n    -- Subquery to find the most recent event for the student\r\n    SELECT TOP 1 \r\n        TC3.SCH_Name\r\n    FROM #TherapistCred TC3\r\n    WHERE TC3.ATT_STUDENT_ID = TC.ATT_STUDENT_ID\r\n      AND TC3.THER_SER = TC.THER_SER\r\n      AND TC3.IEP_IEP_ID = TC.IEP_IEP_ID\r\n      AND (\r\n          (TC3.ESO_SIGNER_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC3.ESO_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49))\r\n          OR (TC3.ATT_Supervisor_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC3.ATT_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49))\r\n          OR (TC3.EV_THERAPIST_ID IS NOT NULL AND TC3.THER_DISC_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49))\r\n      )\r\n    ORDER BY TC3.EV_EVENTEND DESC\r\n) MostRecentEvent\r\nORDER BY TC.ATT_STUDENT_ID, TC.IEP_IEP_ID;\r\n\r\nselect distinct\r\n\r\nSD.DIS_Name District_Name\r\n,SD.School School_Name\r\n,SD.ATT_STUDENT_ID Student_ID\r\n,S.STU_FirstName Student_FirstName\r\n,S.STU_LastName Student_LastName\r\n,S.STU_DateOfBirth Student_DOB\r\n,SD.IEP_IEP_ID IEP_ID\r\n,SD.IEP_BeginningDate\r\n,SD.IEP_EndingDate\r\n,SD.IEP_Service_Type\r\n,SD.Supervisor_Therapist_ID\r\n,T.THE_FirstName Supervisor_FirstName\r\n,T.THE_LastName Supervisor_LastName\r\n,D.DISC_Abbrev Supervisor_Cred\r\n,T.THE_Email Supervisor_Email\r\n,Case \r\n\tWhen T.THE_STELLAR_EMPLOYEE = 1 \r\n\tThen 'Yes' \r\n\tElse 'No' \r\nEnd as StellarTherapist\r\n\r\nfrom #SupervisorData SD\r\njoin STUDENTS S\r\n\ton S.STU_STUDENT_ID = SD.ATT_STUDENT_ID\r\nJoin THERAPISTS T\r\n\ton T.THE_THERAPISTS_ID = SD.Supervisor_Therapist_ID\r\nJOIN CREDHealthLicense THL\r\n    ON THL.CREDHL_THERAPIST_ID = T.THE_THERAPISTS_ID\r\nJOIN CREDLicenseStatus \r\n    ON CREDLicenseStatus_ID = THL.CREDHL_CREDSTAT_ID\r\n    AND CREDLicenseStatus_ID NOT IN (2,4,5,6)\r\nJOIN DISCIPLINES D\r\n    ON DISC_Discipline_ID = THL.CREDHL_LICTYPE\r\n    AND DISC_Discipline_ID IN (13, 5, 8, 49)\r\nWhere SD.SVA_SERVICES_ID IN (@Service)      \r\nAND SD.DIS_DISTRICTS_ID IN (@District)    \r\n--AND TC.EV_EVENTSTART BETWEEN @StartDate AND @EndDate  \r\nAND T.THE_STELLAR_EMPLOYEE IN (@StellarTherapist)    \r\n\r\nOrder by SD.DIS_Name, SD.ATT_STUDENT_ID, SD.IEP_IEP_ID;\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe first part of the query gets all of the therapist credentials by Events, it also pulls most of those student’s information into the first temp table. The second temp table ranks the therapist on who is the student’s supervisor for those events. Since there are Event Therapists, Supervising Therapists, and Therapists that sign off on events I had to determine which therapist needed to be assigned to that student. Each event is different when it comes to the therapist.	SQL query for identifying student supervisor therapists and their credentials	2025-12-04 18:53:01.623+00	2025-12-04 18:53:41.491+00
70	58	2026-01-15T22:10:00.775Z	text/markdown	I think this is done. The results match up with what they're currently getting. Jake reviewed the query and it looked right to him. I'm just waiting on confirmation.	Task completion update	2026-01-15 22:10:29.371+00	2026-01-15 22:10:29.371+00
71	159	2026-03-09T20:36:38.860Z	text/markdown	Fixed in [PR #33](https://github.com/ClearEyeForStellarTherapy/automation/pull/33)\r\n\r\nReleased as a fix: [v1.2.1](https://github.com/ClearEyeForStellarTherapy/automation/releases/tag/v1.2.1)\r\n\r\nThe issue was that we were creating the file with an exclusive lock and then taking too long to write to it and release it. The PowerAutomate file system watcher registered the file but then threw an exception when it tried to read it. I had hoped that PA would have some kind of built-in retry logic, but it didn't work that way, it just failed.\r\n\r\nThe solution is to write the file to a temp folder first and then copy it over.	Fixing PowerAutomate file locking and write issue	2026-03-09 20:39:29.709+00	2026-03-09 20:39:29.709+00
