84	34	2026-02-19T22:34:48.449Z	text/markdown	HollyC  [2:53 PM]\r\n@Michael Gant Can you confirm for me that we are now ok to make changes to the list of Interventions without changing anything on previous events?  Specifically, making some existing ones inactive, changing wording on other one, adding new ones.\r\n\r\nMichael Gant  [5:29 PM]\r\nWell it’s still a little complicated. I have an outstanding task to add an IS_ACTIVE flag to the INTERVENTIONS table. Adding that flag is easy enough, but exactly where to use it may take a little experimentation. There’s a stored proc where we pull all interventions for a therapist (based on services). And it looks like we use that when we bind the interventions list in the popup on the therapy screen. So it makes sense to modify that stored proc to limit to active interventions (once we’ve added that flag).\r\n\r\nBut when I set up the test system, it doesn’t look like I included that proc, and I didn’t get any errors, so I’m thinking we might sometimes be pulling based on previous events for the student and maybe I just never hit the part of the code where we created a brand new one. I need to investigate that a little.\r\n\r\nAt any rate, you’d only be able to actually delete them if they’d never been used. “Positioning/Transfer”, “Seizure Management”, and\r\n“Tracheostomy Care” have never been used.\r\n\r\nThe rest you could mark inactive if you didn’t want them to show up anymore. They would still be attached to the existing events.\r\n\r\nSince we’re dealing with a common reference table for interventions, changing the wording would definitely affect all the previous events. Best option if you need to change the wording but don’t want it to apply retroactively would be to inactivate the old one and create a new one. Not sure how that might affect reporting continuity.\r\n\r\n[5:30 PM]Do you want me to go ahead and add that IS_ACTIVE flag and modify the stored proc to ignore inactive ones?	Updating intervention lists and handling historical data	2026-02-19 22:35:27.242+00	2026-02-19 22:35:27.242+00
85	34	2026-02-20T21:59:40.528Z	text/markdown	HollyC  [11:43 AM]\r\nNo worries - I am following you.  I want to be able to change choices of interventions, level of assistance, results, actions or whatever those 4 tables that are referenced are actually labeled - I think there is some weirdness in the table naming, so finding the ones that are actively used is key.  I think the active/inactive piece sounds like it will work.  As long as we don't lose previous events details, I am good!\r\nMichael Gant  [12:59 PM]\r\nActually it’s like two of the table names are reversed. The RESULTS table (“Level of Assistance” in the UI) contains things like “Independent”, “Supervision”, “Minimal Assist”, etc. The Level_of_Assistance table (“Results” in the UI) contains “0-10% Accuracy”, “10-20% Accuracy”, etc., as well as “Within Normal Limits” and “Not Within Normal Limits - see comments”. The labels in the UI appear to be right. The ACTIONS table contains things like “demonstrated”, “educated”, “facilitated”. It’s labeled “Supports” in the UI. I could see a case for using either name.\r\n\r\nI mentioned yesterday about not being able to delete intervention types that have been used in an event. That’s because there’s a foreign key relationship from INTERVENTIONS (the reference table) to EVENT_INTERVENTIONS (basically, the repeater on the Therapy screen, which contains those four data elements). INTERVENTIONS has a column with the service ID, so each intervention type record can only be used for a single service (“other - see comments” is repeated for each service).\r\n\r\nThe other three are a little more complicated. There’s a ServiceResult table that ties RESULTS records to service IDs, a ServiceLevelOfAssistance table that ties Level_of_Assistance records  to service IDs, and a ServiceActions table that ties ACTIONS records to service IDs. We use those tables to constrain the choices that are displayed in the UI. There’s not actually a foreign key relationship, though (it would have been hard to do that under the circumstances), so there’s nothing at the database that limits those fields on EVENT_INTERVENTIONS to only the defined values. I mention that just to say that we’ll need to be a little more careful with those, because the database would let us delete them without complaining.\r\n\r\nI’ll work on making it where we can “retire” intervention types. That’s the simplest and, I’m guessing, the biggest win. Of the other three, which one should I focus on next?\r\nHollyC  [3:43 PM]\r\nI will use the UI naming:  Actions, Level of Assistance, Results, please.\r\n\r\nDo we ever rename tables?  Or does that break everything??\r\nMichael Gant  [3:47 PM]\r\nRight now I would probably advise against renaming. One of the changes I want to do with the Stellar Docs internal improvements—part of standardizing the data access—is to move database logic out of StellarLibrary.dll and into the main code base. As far as I can find, we don’t have definite source code for that DLL. I’ve been working from a decompiled version of it. But I’ve been careful to avoid changing anything in there. I’ll check and be sure, but I think we’d probably have to make some changes there if we renamed the tables.\r\n\r\nPlus whatever reporting.\r\nHollyC  [4:10 PM]\r\nIt's all good -- I am the one who named all of these and their purpose kept changing as we developed the software!\r\nMichael Gant  [4:12 PM]\r\nWell then I take back all the mean stuff I said back in September when I realized those labels were different from the table names\r\nHollyC  [4:12 PM]\r\nAnd you will add an Active/Non Active designation to each of the other 3 so we can change what the user sees in their drop downs?\r\nMichael Gant  [4:13 PM]\r\nSure I can do that\r\nHollyC  [4:14 PM]\r\nLast thing, is there anyway to make the lists that the users see appear alphabetically going down instead of accross?\r\nMichael Gant  [4:18 PM]\r\nI think so. I see in the code there where it’s got a RepeatDirection="Horizontal" on the radio button control. I’m thinking if we change to to Vertical it might just work. I’m sure we can do it either way, but yeah it looks pretty simple.	Database and UI improvements for intervention data and display options	2026-02-20 21:59:49.851+00	2026-02-20 21:59:49.851+00
