113	76	2026-01-24T15:34:47.018Z	text/markdown	A "quality event" is an abstract term that can include the following:\r\n- measurement of a specific aspect of the subject (thickness, thread count, width, etc.)\r\n- the result of a laboratory test against the subject (strength, flammability, permeability, etc.)\r\n- a defect identified as part of a visual inspection\r\n\r\nQuality events occur as part of a predefined quality management activity. That activity can optionally be associated with a predefined set of measurements and tests.\r\n\r\nQuality events are registered against a "subject", which can be:\r\n- a specific item being manufactured\r\n- a sample derived from a lot, as in a continuous manufacturing process \r\n\r\nEach subject has its own unique identifier	Defining quality events and their subjects	2026-01-24 16:06:58.693+00	2026-01-24 16:06:58.693+00
