131	180	2026-03-24T11:35:44.934Z	text/markdown	***Notes from last onsite***\r\n\r\n\r\n##  Database\r\n1. Determine which SQL agent jobs need to be migrated (vs. left to die)\r\n2. Ensure target server meets or exceeds source server specs\r\n3. Ensure SQL Server on target is installed, running, and accessible from all current clients\r\n4. Take a copy-only backup of TTDS on source; this is not the final copy\r\n5. Restore TTDS to target\r\n6. On target, configure any of the following that exist on source:\r\n    - Logins\r\n        - dbappuser\r\n            - server role public\r\n            - database roles db_datareader and db_datawriter\r\n        - TTC\\llynnadmin\r\n        - TTC\\myetteradmin\r\n    - ~~linked servers~~ \r\n    - SQL agent jobs (not enabled)\r\n        - Cycle Error Log\r\n        - Create new full and incremental backup jobs\r\n    - ~~certificates or keys~~\r\n    - ~~server-level permissions~~\r\n7. Test TTDS from a dev environment against target, ensure all features work\r\n8. Begin downtime\r\n9. Shut down TTDS\r\n10. Take source TTDS offline\r\n11. Take a final copy-only backup of source TTDS\r\n12. Restore TTDS on target, replacing the existing database\r\n13. Update TTDS connection strings\r\n14. Start TTDS\r\n15. Verify TTDS\r\n16. Communicate end of downtime\r\n\r\n## App Servers\r\n1. Configure IIS\r\n2. Install ASP.NET 8 hosting bundle\r\n3. Install AWS CLI\r\n4. Manually copy deployment files for HighlandReporting and TexTechApi\r\n5. Manually configure HighlandReporting and TexTechApi in IIS, using prod URLs\r\n6. Start HighlandReporting and TexTechApi\r\n7. Copy deployment scripts\r\n8. Test run deployment scripts\r\n9. On desktop or laptop, modify hosts file to resolve TTDS aliases to new servers\r\n10. Test direct access to HighlandReporting and TexTechApi\r\n\r\n## Load Balancer\r\n1. Configure IIS\r\n2. Configure URL rewrite module\r\n3. Install AWS CLI\r\n4. Manually copy deployment deployment files for ttds-client\r\n5. Manually configure ttds-client in IIS, using prod URLs\r\n6. Copy URL rewrite rules from source server\r\n7. Manually configure load balancing for HighlandReporting and TexTechApi\r\n8. Copy deployment scripts\r\n9. Test run deployment scripts\r\n10. On desktop or laptop, modify hosts file to resolve TTDS aliases to new server\r\n11. Test access to TTDS\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Log\r\n\r\nkv1-ttdsprod1\r\nEnable IIS feature (Basic auth included but not needed)\r\nInstall ASP.NET 8 hosting bundle\r\nInstall AWS CLI\r\nCopy HighlandReporting and TexTechApi from `\\\\kv1-ssfprpt01\\c$\\inetpub\\wwwroot` to `c:\\inetpub\\wwwroot`\r\nCreate HighlandReporting site\r\n- pointing to C drive\r\n- host name ttds-highlandrpt1.textech-nc.com\r\n- host name ttds.textech-nc.com\r\n- app pool identity (default)\r\nRestart server\r\nCreate TexTechApi site\r\n- pointing to C drive\r\n- host name ttds-api1.textech-nc.com\r\n- host name ttds-api.textech-nc.com\r\n- app pool identity (default)\r\nHighlandReporting working on kv1-ttdsprod1\r\nInstall deployment scripts\r\n\r\nFound bug where searching by nothing at all, only finds a few records\r\n\r\nkv1-ttdsprod2\r\nEnable IIS feature\r\nInstall ASP.NET 8 hosting bundle\r\nCopy apps from kv1-ttdsprod2\r\nSet up apps (2 instead of 1)\r\nInstall AWS CLI\r\nInstall deployment scripts\r\nRestart\r\n\r\nkv1-ttdsload\r\nConfigure server farm ttds.textech-nc.com\r\nConfigure server farm ttds-api.textech-nc.com\r\n\r\nkv1-ttdsprod1\r\nGrant local IIS_IUSRS group full control on c:\\ProgramData\\HighlandReporting and TexTechApi\r\n\r\nOther notes\r\nI had to remove the CORS and stuff from the web.configs, but actually I think the project GUID at the bottom was the real culprit\r\n\r\nThe server farm stuff was actually a lot simpler than I had previously thought. All you need is the server farm, not any instances of the actual applications. The trick is to configure the URL rewrite rules at the server level to map to the correct server farm based on the `{HTTP_HOST}`.\r\n\r\nImprovements vs previous config:\r\n- server farm is simpler\r\n- applications are running under the app pool identity, not a specific user ID\r\n\r\nkv1-ttdstest1\r\nEnable IIS\r\nInstall hosting bundle\r\nRestart\r\nInstall SQL Server\r\n- default options\r\n- mixed auth\r\n- sa password same as TTDS Admin\r\n- TTC\\llynadmin is sysadmin\r\nRestart\r\nInstall SSMS\r\nCopy HighlandReporting and TexTechApi from kv1-ttdsprod1 and change settings\r\n- database user is same as production\r\nAccidentally copied onpremtest build of ttds-client to kv1-ttdsload\r\nRestored production build of ttds-client on kv1-ttdsload from kv1-app02\r\nInstal URL rewrite module\r\nCopy web.config from kv1-ttdsload to get routing rules\r\n\r\nUpdated load balancing on kv1-ttdsload to point to ttds-highlandrpt3 and 4 and ttds-api3 and 4 instead of 1 and 2, as a test (didn't work initially because those DNS aliases are apparently configured in a loop)\r\n\r\nConfigured bindings for 3 and 4 aliases on PROD1 and PROD2\r\n\r\nStopped default website on both app servers (had already stopped it on test)\r\n\r\nCreated table DataProtectionKeys\r\n\r\nPublished updated version of HighlandReporting to PROD1 and PROD2\r\n\r\nUpdated connection strings in HighlandReporting on PROD1 and PROD2 to include TrustServerCertificate=true (necessary because I updated the EF packages to .NET 8)\r\n\r\nSet up dbappuser in test database with db_datareader and db_datawriter database roles	Notes from last onsite	2026-03-24 11:36:35.203962+00	2026-03-24 11:36:35.203962+00
