133	180	2026-03-24T13:52:20.486Z	text/markdown	***Migration log***\r\n\r\n## Events\r\n0940: I generated scripts for putting the old database, in single-user, taking a backup, and restoring the backup\r\n0950: While working on the scripts, I realized that the new database had been created with the files on the C drive instead of E and F. I'm moving those now.\r\n1020: I moved the files for the new TTDS to `E:\\SQLData\\TTDS.mdf` and `F:\\SQLLogs\\TTDS.ldf`. I also changed the logical names from `Highland` and `Highland_log` to `TTDS` and `TTDS_log`. For this to work, I also had to grant `NT Service\\MSSSQLSERVER` full control on the E and F drives.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\nThe database is in `SIMPLE` recovery mode. Combined with the image-level backup and the RPO tied to that backup, there's really no need for a database-specific backup process.\r\n\r\nMigration is done. I ended up having to deploy the latest version of TTDS.\r\n- daily inspection totals fails sometimes, probably timeout-related\r\n- the deployment pipeline is broken\r\n- there doesn't seem to be a way to configure AWS profiles for use with IIS, need to find an alternative\r\n- need to set some query timeouts and keep working on performance	Database migration log with events and notes	2026-03-24 13:57:12.328027+00	2026-03-24 18:11:19.34184+00
