171	215	2026-05-08T18:46:26.397Z	text/markdown	Larry is going to check with the operations team about this.\r\n\r\nThe UI input is actually backed by three fields in the database. If the input matches the "laminate" regex `^(?<workOrderNumber>\\d{6})(?<rollNumber>\\d{3})$`—indicating that the current pass is an additional layer (a laminate) on top of the previous layer indicated by the work order and roll number, we extract those values and store them in `PreviousStepWorkOrderNumber` and `PreviousStepRollNumber` on the `LabRoll`. If it's any other combination of letters and numbers <= 20 long, we store it in the `GreigeNumber` field, indicating that the current pass is applying coating to a greige (uncoated) roll.\r\n\r\nI've got questions in to them about whether the system is allowing the 10-digit inputs as it should (and store in the `GreigeNumber` field), and whether that's causing any downstream problems for them.	Parsing UI input for LabRoll laminate and greige numbers	2026-05-08 18:51:12.698868+00	2026-05-08 18:51:12.698868+00
