174	212	2026-05-11T21:46:34.682Z	text/markdown	Today I added the first part of the disposition form. I still need to add the rules for enabling and disabling the controls. I also need to add the comments and the submission and refresh logic.\r\n\r\nI got some AI help with the disposition summary. The response was pretty good but I need to analyze and test it thoroughly. Here was the prompt I used:\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nHelp me reason on this. I've got this class.\r\n\r\n```c-sharp\r\n#nullable enable\r\n\r\nusing System;\r\nusing System.Collections.Generic;\r\nusing System.Linq;\r\nusing System.Threading.Tasks;\r\n\r\nnamespace HighlandReporting.Models.V2\r\n{\r\n    public class MRBReview\r\n    {\r\n        public required string WorkOrderNumber { get; set; }\r\n        public int RollNumber { get; set; }\r\n        public required string LocationSequenceCode { get; set; }\r\n        public int SampleIndex { get; set; }\r\n        public DateTime ReviewDate { get; set; }\r\n        public string? ManufacturingReviewer { get; set; }\r\n        public DateTime? ManufacturingReviewDate { get; set; }\r\n        public string? ManufacturingDisposition { get; set; }\r\n        public string? ManufacturingRestyleAsStyleNumber { get; set; }\r\n        public string? ManufacturingRetestInstructions { get; set; }\r\n        public int? ManufacturingRestyleApplyToRollsBefore { get; set; }\r\n        public int? ManufacturingRestyleApplyToRollsAfter { get; set; }\r\n        public int? ManufacturingScrapApplyToRollsBefore { get; set; }\r\n        public int? ManufacturingScrapApplyToRollsAfter { get; set; }\r\n        public string? QualityReviewer { get; set; }\r\n        public DateTime? QualityReviewDate { get; set; }\r\n        public string? QualityDisposition { get; set; }\r\n        public string? QualityRestyleAsStyleNumber { get; set; }\r\n        public string? QualityRetestInstructions { get; set; }\r\n        public int? QualityRestyleApplyToRollsBefore { get; set; }\r\n        public int? QualityRestyleApplyToRollsAfter { get; set; }\r\n        public int? QualityScrapApplyToRollsBefore { get; set; }\r\n        public int? QualityScrapApplyToRollsAfter { get; set; }\r\n        public string? OverrideReviewer { get; set; }\r\n        public DateTime? OverrideReviewDate { get; set; }\r\n        public string? OverrideDisposition { get; set; }\r\n        public string? OverrideRestyleAsStyleNumber { get; set; }\r\n        public string? OverrideRetestInstructions { get; set; }\r\n        public int MRBReviewId { get; set; }\r\n        public int? OverrideRestyleApplyToRollsBefore { get; set; }\r\n        public int? OverrideRestyleApplyToRollsAfter { get; set; }\r\n        public int? OverrideScrapApplyToRollsBefore { get; set; }\r\n        public int? OverrideScrapApplyToRollsAfter { get; set; }\r\n       \r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI need to derive a "disposition summary". \r\n\r\nOverride always wins.\r\nIf override is null, manufacturing and quality have to agree.\r\nPossible dispositions are:\r\n\r\nRelease\r\nScrap\r\nRestyle\r\nReswatch\r\nRecheck\r\nRelease means that no further action is needed.\r\nScrap means that the roll cannot be used. Optionally, the reviewer can specify that n rolls before and/or after the test roll should also be scrapped.\r\nRestyle generally means cutting off the part of the roll (either length or width) so that it conforms to style x instead of its original style. This disposition can also be applied to n rolls before or after.\r\nReswatch means to create a new swatch and test against that. Recheck means to run the test against the previous swatch. On Retest, the review has the option to provide additional instructions.\r\nIf the disposition is final (override, or manufacturing = quality), I want to simply display the disposition and related information. Possible outcomes include:\r\n\r\nRelease\r\nScrap roll {current roll}\r\nScrap rolls {current roll minus rolls before} to {current roll plus rolls after}\r\nRestyle roll {current roll} as {new style}\r\nRestyle rolls {current roll minus rolls before} to {current roll plus rolls after} as {new style}\r\nReswatch\r\nRetest: no instructions provided\r\nRetest with instructions: {retest instructions}\r\nIf there's a partial disposition, I want to show what's there, prefixed by Mfg and Qlty. A few  examples:\r\n\r\nMfg: Release; Qlty: Pending\r\nMfg: Scrap roll {n}; Qlty: Release\r\nMfg: Pending; Qlty: Reswatch\r\nOf course, there are many possible variations of that.\r\nAnother possible case is that the dispositions match but the before/after, restyle style, and/or retest instructions don't. In those cases, I want to show the agreed disposition but a warning, as in:\r\n\r\nScrap: Mfg and Qlty differ on rolls\r\nRetest: Mfg and Qlty differ on instructions\r\nAnd so forth.\r\nI can think of a long boring brute-force way of doing this but I'm hoping to find a slightly more maintainable algorithm.	Defining MRB Review Disposition Summary Logic	2026-05-11 21:48:34.636068+00	2026-05-11 21:48:34.636068+00
175	215	2026-05-12T17:10:49.973Z	text/markdown	The operations team reported back that the 10th digit was being truncated. I investigated and found that the actual pattern is `^(\\d{6})(\\d{3})[A-Z0-9]?$`. I think I remember the conversation and the reason why we added that tenth letter or digit: it's kind of an optional suffix. Unfortunately it makes it impossible to actually use 10-digit numbers.\r\n\r\nMy suggested work-around was to prefix the number with an "M" or something. They had actually already tried prefixing it with "00" but report that it didn't work. I can't tell why it wouldn't have worked. I asked them to send examples.\r\n\r\nIf they actually need to be able to input the 10-digit number and not have it be treated as a laminate style, we'll need to decide whether the laminate "suffix" can always be letters, or if not, we'll either need to try to decide based on the product type of the work order's style, or add a UI element to allow the user to clarify the intent.	Truncation of 10-digit numbers due to regex pattern	2026-05-12 17:14:13.996577+00	2026-05-12 17:14:13.996577+00
