53	46	2026-02-27T15:12:40.632Z	text/markdown	# Migration Notes\r\n\r\nThis is meant to be a running note where I update the results of each migration.\r\n\r\n## Abandon\r\nThe abandon page is just a way of abandoning the session.\r\nI don't see where we ever call it.\r\nI think we could probably safely remove it, but a little more research is needed.\r\n\r\n## AddStudent\r\nThis is called from a button on the home page.\r\nIt works fine.\r\nBut it's probably worth finding out whether adding students is normally done in hub instead.\r\nSuggestions for improvement:\r\n- calendar control for DOB is not super useful since you have to click back month by month to get to a reasonable DOB for a school-age child (at least 60 clicks)\r\n- validation message "Save Failed" isn't super helpful\r\n- unless we use this form to add many students at a time, it would be better to close the form and maybe do a toast notification that it succeeded\r\n\r\n## Attendance\r\nThis is a fairly complex page, and as far as I can tell, it's only called in a very specific circumstance, which may never happen.\r\nFrom `CalTherapy.ascx`, on initial page load, it runs `usp_sel_EVENTDETAIL`,\r\nwhich is a very weird stored proc that actually does a `UNION` and returns two rows (sometimes at least) for the same event.\r\nBut we're only reading the first row.\r\nAnd only in cases where the `EV_ATTENDANCE_STATUS` is null, then we redirect from `CalTherapy.ascx` to `Attendance.aspx`.\r\nBut that doesn't make sense either, because `Attendance.aspx` isn't really a full page, it's clearly meant to run within the iframe,\r\nbut maybe that's where that redirect happens (I'm a little confused on that point).\r\nMy gut is that we never use Attendance.aspx anymore, only CalAttendance.aspx.\r\nBut I haven't been able to prove that.\r\nThere are a few stored procs that I had to add to test to get this page to work.\r\nThey may not actually be needed anymore:\r\n- `usp_parmsel_ATTENDANCE_ByEventD` (sic)\r\n- `usp_sel_ABSENT_REASON`\r\n- `usp_sel_TREATMENT_CODES`\r\n- `usp_parmsel_STUDENTS_BySchoolID`\r\n- `usp_upd_EVENT_ByEventID`\r\n- `usp_parmsel_CheckBeginAssessment` (this one uses an `exec` in production; I rewrote it in test)\r\n\r\nAlso, when it is called, it sets two query string parameters: `&EV_ATTENDANCE_STATUS=False&VerifyAttendance=True`, which aren't used for anything.\r\n\r\n## AttendanceNeeded\r\nThis one is called from the main page, the red "Take Attendance" button in the middle.\r\n\r\nIt was fairly simple to migrate.\r\n\r\n## AttendanceToday\r\nThis is called from the main page, the green "Review & Submit" button in the middle.\r\n\r\n## CaseLoadManagement\r\nThis is called from the main page, side menu.\r\n\r\nIt's a bit of a snowflake. It's the only place where we use Bootstrap, for the purpose of using the Bootstrap modal instead of the jQuery UI one.\r\nIt also used a different version of jQuery and a unique way of loading the libraries onto  the page.\r\nI reworked it to use vanilla JS and to load Bootstrap from CDN inline. \r\nNot a great solution, but an improvement.\r\n\r\n## ChangePassword\r\nCalled from the main page, top nav menu\r\n\r\n## ContactUs\r\nCalled from the main page, "CHANGE FORM" on top nav menu\r\n\r\n## DetailsNeeded\r\nI migrated this one but I can't actually see where it's being used. I had to add the stored proc `usp_parmsel_EVENTS_Detail_Needed` to get this to work, so that proc may also not be needed.\r\n\r\n## Documents\r\nCalled from main page, top nav menu. I also migrated all the documents.\r\n\r\n## GlobalAttendance\r\nThe only non-commented place where this is called is from a button handler for `btnBuildCalendar` on `StellarHome`. But that button doesn't seem to exist. I don't think this page is called.\r\n\r\n## GlobalErrorPage\r\nThis is called from `Global.asax` as the last-resort handler for errors other than `HttpException`\r\n\r\n## GroupManagement\r\nMigrated but doesn't seem to be called from anywhere.\r\n\r\n## Nursing\r\nMigrated. Not called from anywhere. Added stored procs `cusp_sel_Districts_Nursing` and `cusp_parmsel_TREATMENT_CODES`.\r\n\r\n## Reports\r\nMigrated. Called from the `StellarAdmin` master page.\r\n\r\n## Student Assessments\r\nMigrated. Not called from anywhere. Code-behind had been misspelled "Assesssments".\r\n\r\n## Student Attendance Report\r\nMigrated. Called from `Reports.aspx`.\r\n\r\n## Student Attendance Report By Date Preview\r\nMigrated. Called from `Student Attendance Report`.\r\n\r\n## Student Details\r\nMigrated. Called from home page. Added stored procs `acusp_parmsel_Therapist_School_Assignments`, `acusp_DISTRICTS_Select`, and `acusp_DISTRICTS_Select`.\r\n\r\n## Students Not On Schedule\r\nMigrated. Called from Reports. Also called from a button handler on Student Details, but there's no button.\r\n\r\n## Students On Schedule\r\nMigrated. Called from Reports. Also called from a button handler on Student Details, but there's no button.\r\n\r\n## Therapist Reports\r\nMigrated. Link on main page. Uses obsolete WebViewer component.\r\n\r\n## Therapist Students\r\nMigrated. "View Case Load" button on main page.\r\n\r\n## Therapists Intervention New\r\nMigrated. Used in primary documentation workflow.\r\n\r\n## UserControls/Assessment\r\nMigrated. Called from Student Assessments (which doesn't seem to be called from anywhere). Included stored procs `usp_sel_AreaOfAssessment`, `usp_parmsel_GetStudentAssessments`, and `usp_parmsel_GetAssessmentForAssessments`.\r\n\r\n## UserControls/SessionHistory\r\nMigrated. Called from Student Details\r\n\r\n## UserControls/Services\r\nMigrated. Called from Student Details.\r\n\r\n## UserControls/ucDocuments\r\nMigrated. Called from Student Details.\r\n\r\n## UserControls/ucGroupEntry\r\nMigrated. Not called from anywhere.\r\n\r\n## UserControls/Goals\r\nMigrated. Called from Student Details.\r\n	Migration notes for application pages and controls	2026-02-27 15:13:59.861+00	2026-05-22 18:22:15.443852+00
