190	107	2026-05-20T21:18:24.969Z	text/markdown	This one has turned out to be really messy. It requires us to include the WebViewer control, which is no longer maintained by Microsoft and isn't available as a (legit) NuGet package. It also includes a bunch of added views, procs, a UDF, and some configuration data.\r\n\r\nI've got the first report sort of working (with no data). Next step is to get the rest of the reports working, which will require some additional procs, etc., but hopefully won't require much more in the way of code changes.\r\n\r\nWe definitely should consider the future direction of these reports and how to make them available in a supported and maintainable way.	Challenges and future direction for a legacy reporting system	2026-05-20 21:20:46.911192+00	2026-05-20 21:20:46.911192+00
191	115	2026-05-21T21:10:19.723Z	text/markdown	I migrated this one over but I need to spin up the test environment on my next working day and make sure it works.	Pending migration testing	2026-05-21 21:10:50.195056+00	2026-05-21 21:10:50.195056+00
200	234	2026-06-15T20:43:26.874Z	text/markdown	My response to Stephanie:\r\n\r\n**Second page** yeah I agree that the too-long email address is pushing us to the next page. I was trying to match the existing layout as closely as possible. Do you think it would be OK if I made a few small adjustments? For example, we could make the name a little narrower and the email a little wider and still probably have plenty of room for both. Or if we needed to, we could probably make the giant header at the top just a little smaller to allow a little more room for the school district, and reduce the vertical space in that top-right box a little, and cut out a little space above the "Did you assess..." line, to give us a little more breathing room at the bottom.	Discussing document layout adjustments	2026-06-15 20:43:51.969321+00	2026-06-15 20:43:51.969321+00
201	235	2026-06-15T20:45:09.789Z	text/markdown	My response to Stephanie:\r\n\r\n**Referral status** right now we're excluding IEPs if there's a referral (matched on student, service, and date range) with a status of "RECEIVED SIGNED" (2). I'll add "SENT-WAITING ON RESPONSE" (9), "Moved out of District" (10), and "Inactive Student" (6). That will leave the following statuses in the "don't exclude based on" list:\r\n\r\n- IEP not signed by therapist (1)\r\n- SIGNATURE PAGE NOT FOUND (3)\r\n- REFERRING THERAPIST NOT FOUND (4)\r\n- SEE ADDITIONAL INFORMATION (5)\r\n- IEP Order Not Needed (7)\r\n- RECEIVED SIGNED - Needs Creds (8)\r\n- Different therapist provider (11)\r\n- Did not service student during IEP year (12)\r\n- Know nothing about student (13)\r\n- IEP NOT SIGNED (14)\r\n- Inactive Therapist in District (15)	Referral status updates for IEP exclusion criteria	2026-06-15 20:45:27.207645+00	2026-06-15 20:45:27.207645+00
202	236	2026-06-15T20:46:06.927Z	text/markdown	My response to Stephanie:\r\n\r\n**Limit by district** not a problem. There are a few ways we can define that interface. The simplest for me would be to add a `--districts` option on the command line, which would accept a comma-separated list of district IDs, something like `--districts 31,38,189`. That would require you to look up (or happen to know) the district IDs, but it's simple to code. We could make it accept a list of district names, or even a file containing a list of district names, to make it a little more user-friendly, sort of, except that the name would have to be spelled exactly the same as in the database—I mean, we could implement a "did you mean" feature, but it would be complicated—so you might end up having to look it up anyway. Can we stick with the IDs?	Command-line option for district ID filtering	2026-06-15 20:46:36.520701+00	2026-06-15 20:46:36.520701+00
203	57	2026-06-15T20:46:55.685Z	text/markdown	Message from Stephanie based on results from the first batch of therapy orders:\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n@Michael Gant we finally got through the last round of IEP Therapy Orders with your updated generation process. We have a few things to see if they can be tweaked before next school year. We will plan to do our first send out in September.\r\n\r\n- Sometimes the PDF that is generated is 2 pages instead of 1--Teralyn believes it is because the email address is too long and splits the info down a line creating that 2nd page. I have an example added. \r\n- We found that if the last event was absent, then the student wasn't picked up for order creation. If the last session was absent it should continue looking for a present visit and generate the order. \r\n- Query seems to be going with most seen. Should be last seen therapist. Sometimes a new therapist is assigned and the previous therapist will refuse even if they’ve seen them the most because they are no longer the assigned therapist.\r\n- We LOVE being able to do a mass generation of orders but we would also love the ability to limit the districts (Sometimes we need to do a special send out and we don't want to do all) Can you have a process that Jake can do that he can specify certain districts to be generated?\r\n- Double check to make sure that we aren't generating orders for the same IEP if they have one of the following statuses: ‘sent-waiting on response’, ‘moved out of district’ and ‘inactive student’\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI created a [bug](/work-items/234) for the second page issue and stories for the [districts](/work-items/236) and [status codes](/work-items/235).	Feedback and issues for IEP Therapy Orders generation process	2026-06-15 20:50:50.571103+00	2026-06-15 20:50:50.571103+00
204	226	2026-06-18T21:14:49.229Z	text/markdown	This is mostly working. The last steps:\r\n\r\n- existing results (including those just submitted) can't be edited\r\n- display an error if the result isn't accepted for some reason	Last steps for results feature	2026-06-18 21:16:53.865093+00	2026-06-18 21:16:53.865093+00
