210	231	2026-06-19T21:56:51.132Z	text/markdown	Sent this to Larry. No response yet, I'm assuming he ran it and it worked.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nGot it. Here’s the script:\r\n\r\n```sql\r\nbegin transaction\r\n\r\ninsert TestDefinition (TestName, KVWI, CertificateName, ValueTypeCode, IsCoatedWeightTest)\r\nselect 'Elongation @ 2lbs - Bias', KVWI, 'Elongation @ 2lbs - Bias', ValueTypeCode, IsCoatedWeightTest\r\nfrom TestDefinition\r\nwhere TestName = 'Elongation Bias'\r\n\r\nupdate Observation\r\n    set TestName = 'Elongation @ 2lbs - Bias'\r\nwhere TestName = 'Elongation Bias'\r\n\r\nupdate StyleTestConfiguration\r\nset TestName = 'Elongation @ 2lbs - Bias'\r\nwhere TestName = 'Elongation Bias'\r\n\r\ndelete from TestDefinition\r\nwhere TestName = 'Elongation Bias'\r\n\r\ncommit transaction\r\n```\r\n\r\nI ran this against my local dev and it had the expected effect, but that’s a very old and heavily modified version of a production backup from years ago. You might think about running this against your on-premise test database first. Or take a backup of production.\r\n\r\nI mean, it should be pretty straightforward, but at the same time, it’s probably updating a lot of records.\r\n\r\nI’ll be at my desk for the next couple of hours in case anything comes up.	SQL script to rename a test definition	2026-06-19 21:57:30.479151+00	2026-06-19 21:57:30.479151+00
211	231	2026-06-19T21:58:07.659Z	text/markdown	Original message was:\r\n\r\nMike,\r\n \r\nI have been asked to change the name of a current test method.  The current method is “Elongation Bias”, and Andrew wants it to be “Elongation @ 2lbs – Bias”\r\n \r\nThere is a TestName field and a CertificateName field that appear to be the same.\r\n \r\nI assume that I can change it with:\r\nupdate TestDefinition \r\n              set TestName = “Elongation @ 2lbs – Bias”\r\n \r\nbut my where clause could be:\r\n \r\nwhere CertificateName = “Elongation Bias”\r\n \r\nbut then I would have to change CertificateName field to “Elongation @ 2lbs – Bias” as well so I guess my next update routine can be the opposite of this one.\r\n \r\nPlease advise, I don’t want to mess up the TestDefinition table.	SQL update advice for changing test method name	2026-06-19 21:58:21.668725+00	2026-06-19 21:58:21.668725+00
